114
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:31,460
And Michael Scott's dealing with all of the mixed emotions

115
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:33,680
and guilt of being the one that hit her with the car

116
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,820
and also never wanting to be wrong,

117
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:38,000
and so trying to justify all of the things

118
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,600
that have happened.

119
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:41,580
And with a mix of complicated emotions

120
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,700
and motivations, guilt,

121
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:47,060
and the thing about Michael Scott

122
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:49,680
is even when he's acting like a total buffoon,

123
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:51,780
you can see deep down inside

124
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:53,120
that he actually does care.

125
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:55,560
And so with this mixed emotions

126
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,840
of kindness, compassion, and also guilt,

127
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:01,280
and also just a desire to be praised,

128
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:05,240
he organizes the, here we go,

129
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,860
Michael Scott's Dunder Mifflin,

130
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:11,000
Scranton Meredith Palmer Memorial Celebrity Rabies Awareness

131
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,840
Pro-Am Fun Run Race for the Cure.

132
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:17,900
As you can see the succinct title on the T-shirt,

133
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:23,080
he organizes this very long titled race

134
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:25,900
in order to raise money for rabies,

135
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,820
a disease that has already been cured.

136
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:32,340
So, although the plot of this episode,

137
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:33,740
as with the entire show,

138
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,140
is just blatant hyperbolic satire,

139
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:38,880
I think it reveals something that is typically true

140
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:42,940
of human beings as it relates to the idea of serving others.

141
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,480
And that is we come to service

142
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,580
with this mixed bag of motivations.

143
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:50,620
We come to service with this idea

144
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:52,280
of wanting in some ways

145
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,900
to kind of earn favor before God.

146
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:57,700
We wanna demonstrate to God and to others

147
00:06:57,700 --> 00:07:00,840
that we are a person that is worthy of praise

148
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,380
because we are willing to sacrifice and serve others.

149
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:04,680
Sometimes we do it out of guilt,

150
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:06,980
out of a, I'm gonna pay off the bad things I've done

151
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:08,500
with the good things that I've done.

152
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:11,480
And service is this thing where it's really easy

153
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:14,660
for us to do the right thing for the wrong reasons.

154
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:18,520
Anybody resonate with that idea this morning?

155
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,860
Either out of guilt or regret

156
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,840
or a desire to make a name for ourselves

157
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:24,780
before God and others,

158
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:27,160
we can easily make a habit of doing the right thing

159
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,360
for the wrong reasons,

160
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:30,200
which will not give us the results

161
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:32,760
that Jesus is wanting for us

162
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,120
when he invites us to serve.

163
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,120
He invites us to serve

164
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:38,160
because in truly serving him

165
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:39,620
out of a love for God

166
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,660
and a love for our neighbor,

167
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:42,680
we will experience the abundant life

168
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:45,300
that glorifies God and that gives us peace.

169
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,660
But there's a way in which we can pursue service

170
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:49,820
without getting those results.

171
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:52,060
And so what I wanna do this morning

172
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:53,680
is I wanna look at an example

173
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,800
of Jesus serving his disciples

174
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:59,120
and doing so in such a way

175
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,580
that sets an example for us,

176
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:04,900
that teaches us what genuine kingdom service looks like

177
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:07,400
and it equips us moving forward

178
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:10,220
to serve in the same way that Jesus did.

179
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:10,960
So if you have your Bibles,

180
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,780
you wanna turn to John chapter 13.

181
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:16,940
John chapter 13 is gonna be our text this morning

182
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:19,280
and in it, we will see Jesus set an example,

183
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,180
but it's also not just him setting an example,

184
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:24,980
it's him giving an object lesson to his disciples.

185
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,860
It's intended both to teach them something

186
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,500
intellectually, emotionally,

187
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:32,660
and also send them out in the future

188
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:36,500
with the same type of service that Jesus serves them.

189
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:39,380
One where we do the right things for the right reasons.

190
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:43,280
And the curriculum that we're following,

191
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:45,040
the focus on this week

192
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,380
is the idea of serving in hiddenness.

193
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:52,440
Like we start this discipline of service in hiddenness

194
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:55,980
because when we can do it sacrificially for no praise,

195
00:08:55,980 --> 00:09:01,640
for no pride, for no other acceptance,

196
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,860
for no other benefit

197
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:04,600
other than just to sacrificially serve,

198
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:06,440
if we build our service on that,

199
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:09,180
it is in the hidden places where we serve

200
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:11,240
that we can be formed into a person

201
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:13,440
that can go out and serve in the public square

202
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,240
and do it for the right reason.

203
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:16,160
That make sense?

204
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:20,540
All right, so John chapter 13, starting in verse one,

205
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:24,100
says, it was just before the Passover festival.

206
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:27,520
Jesus knew that the hour had come for him

207
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:30,020
to leave this world and go to the Father.

208
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:38,260
I love that idea that this is right before

209
00:09:38,260 --> 00:09:39,440
he's about to go to the cross.

210
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:41,680
And it says he knew the hour had come.

211
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:42,880
What hour had come?

212
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:45,100
The hour for him to go to the cross?

213
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:48,300
No, he says the hour for him to leave this world

214
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:49,360
and go to his Father.

215
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,160
Like even in the midst of him going to the cross,

216
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:55,000
his focus is on reunion with the Father.

217
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,940
His focus is on the kingdom to come.

218
00:09:57,940 --> 00:10:00,540
Having loved his own who were in the world,

219
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:01,980
he loved them to the end.

220
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:05,060
The evening meal was in progress

221
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:07,400
and the devil had already prompted Judas,

222
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,660
the son of Simon Iscariot,

223
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,680
to betray Jesus.

224
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,000
Jesus knew that the Father had put all things

225
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,140
under his power and that he had come from God

226
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:18,200
and was returning to God.

227
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,340
He had this kingdom perspective.

228
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:22,720
And because of that, it says,

229
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:24,700
he got up from the meal.

230
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,820
He took off his outer clothing.

231
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:29,360
He wrapped a towel around his waist.

232
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:32,720
After that, he poured water into a basin

233
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:35,780
and he began to wash his disciples' feet,

234
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:39,980
drying them with the towel that was wrapped around him.

235
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:42,560
Jumping to verse 12, it says,

236
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:45,040
when he had finished washing their feet,

237
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:48,160
he put on his clothes and returned to his place.

238
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,520
And he said to his disciples,

239
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:52,500
do you understand what I have done for you?

240
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:55,860
You call me teacher and Lord and rightly so,

241
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,180
for this is what I am.

242
00:10:57,180 --> 00:11:00,500
Now that I, your Lord and teacher,

243
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,980
have washed your feet,

244
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:04,980
you should also wash one another's feet.

245
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,180
I have set for you an example

246
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,040
that you should do as I have done for you.

247
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,400
Very truly, I tell you,

248
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,940
no servant is greater than his master,

249
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:17,060
nor is a messenger greater than the one who sent him.

250
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:20,360
Now that you know these things,

251
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:23,980
you will be blessed if you do them.

252
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:29,120
So the disciples who are participating

253
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:30,580
in the Passover meal with Jesus

254
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,880
just hours before he will be crucified

255
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:36,280
are doing something really interesting.

256
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,940
We don't have it in the context in John,

257
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:39,900
but we have it in the context of Luke.

258
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:42,160
Luke records that during this very dinner,

259
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:46,360
the disciples whom Jesus loved behind closed doors

260
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:49,080
who are celebrating the Passover feast

261
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,640
that's supposed to focus their attention

262
00:11:50,640 --> 00:11:53,340
on God's deliverance in their lives,

263
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:54,620
they are in a debate

264
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,780
over who is the greatest among them in the kingdom.

265
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:59,880
Sound like Christians?

266
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,480
Right?

267
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,340
So they're debating over

268
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:05,020
who is the greatest among them in the kingdom,

269
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,780
and I think that it's in that context

270
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,840
that we have to put Jesus doing this object lesson,

271
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:10,960
this parable for them.

272
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:14,800
He is showing them the definition to that question,

273
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,100
the answer to the question

274
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,460
of who is the greatest among you,

275
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:18,540
and what does it look like

276
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:22,080
to be the greatest among people in the kingdom?

277
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:25,300
And it's not that they aren't willing to serve, right?

278
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,600
The disciples have followed Jesus

279
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:27,720
for three years at this point,

280
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,760
sacrificially giving up so much,

281
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,900
giving up their careers and their life,

282
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,360
and they have followed Jesus.

283
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,200
They are willing to serve.

284
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:36,080
They know Jesus.

285
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,040
They know who he is.

286
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:37,960
They know what he's about.

287
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,940
It's not that they're opposed to sacrificial service.

288
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,920
It's that they're primarily focused right now

289
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,940
on the rewards that they will receive

290
00:12:44,940 --> 00:12:46,500
for the things that they've given up.

291
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:50,400
It's in this very moment that they are like,

292
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:51,260
yeah, we'll serve.

293
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:52,860
We'll give our lives for this kingdom,

294
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:55,120
but what do we get in return?

295
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:59,560
Just like Michael Scott,

296
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:02,280
and like most of us in the room,

297
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:04,440
even in our willingness to serve others,

298
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,220
oftentimes somewhere deep down inside of us,

299
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:09,960
we are thinking about how we might benefit from it.

300
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:13,320
And it's in that moment

301
00:13:13,320 --> 00:13:16,540
that the incarnate Son of God

302
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:19,220
models for them what true service

303
00:13:19,220 --> 00:13:20,540
in the kingdom of God looks like.

304
00:13:20,540 --> 00:13:24,620
He does the unspeakable,

305
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:27,320
a service that I read scholars say

306
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,920
Jewish slaves wouldn't even typically perform.

307
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:33,900
So this is a cultural thing that would happen

308
00:13:33,900 --> 00:13:35,980
because they walked the streets

309
00:13:35,980 --> 00:13:39,560
that were filled with dirt, mud, and human feces.

310
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:42,980
Oftentimes they would have Gentile servants

311
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,880
waiting at the door to wash the feet

312
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:45,940
before you go to a meal

313
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:48,000
because you don't wanna sit at the table

314
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,580
where you are reclining with your feet

315
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,800
next to the head of the person you're sitting next to

316
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,060
with feet that are disgusting.

317
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:56,800
And so the servants would do this.

318
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:00,260
And apparently for this reason,

319
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,020
and I'm guessing that Jesus made sure

320
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,660
that it wasn't organized this way,

321
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:05,300
nobody washed the disciples' feet.

322
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,720
And it's in the midst of the dinner,

323
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:10,280
Jesus gets up and he lives out a parable

324
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:12,020
about service in the kingdom of God

325
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:13,480
to his disciples who are debating

326
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,080
who is the greatest among them.

327
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,840
Are we tracking?

328
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:22,580
And it's impossible for us to wrap our minds

329
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:25,260
how culturally shocking this action would have been.

330
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:31,740
I racked my brain for the last few days

331
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,980
trying to come up with an illustration

332
00:14:32,980 --> 00:14:35,060
that meets our cultural expectations

333
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:37,720
where we can imagine how audacious it would be

334
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,960
that Jesus did this thing.

335
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:42,140
And I just didn't have one.

336
00:14:42,140 --> 00:14:44,000
I don't think there is one

337
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,820
that really illustrates for us

338
00:14:46,820 --> 00:14:49,280
what it is that Jesus is doing right now.

339
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:51,960
And he's not just doing it for his faithful disciples.

340
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,020
He does it to Peter,

341
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:55,320
who he knows is about to betray him three times.

342
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,520
And he does it to Judas,

343
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:59,140
who he knows is the reason he is about to be killed.

344
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:01,500
And what's interesting to me is later,

345
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,020
Jesus tells them,

346
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:05,120
somebody's gonna betray me tonight.

347
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,120
And they're like, who is it?

348
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:11,060
So like Jesus so loved Judas in the midst of this

349
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:13,300
that there wasn't a passive aggressive,

350
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,920
like scrubbing his feet a little bit harder, right?

351
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:17,160
Like the whole room was like,

352
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:18,600
who is gonna betray you?

353
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:22,280
Jesus is lovingly washing the feet of his enemy,

354
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,860
the person that's going to betray him,

355
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:27,360
his best friend that's going to deny him three times.

356
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,300
And there is nothing in this for Jesus.

357
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:30,980
He's behind closed doors.

358
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:33,400
The action is done to a group of people

359
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,480
that have already given up everything to follow him.

360
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:39,200
He isn't doing this for any other reason

361
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:41,180
but to teach them and to equip them,

362
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,520
to teach them how much he loves them,

363
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:47,720
how deeply he is,

364
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,920
everything in him is for them.

365
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:55,140
He does this so that they get this idea in their bones

366
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,600
because they are about to have to,

367
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,880
they are about to be invited

368
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,980
to give up everything for him.

369
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:03,740
And you can't do that out of a place

370
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:06,460
of not knowing how loved you are from God.

371
00:16:06,460 --> 00:16:08,420
So Jesus models this for him.

372
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:10,680
He teaches them so that they can understand it.

373
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,580
And then he sets an example for them

374
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,400
so that they will do it.

375
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:15,640
I love verse 17.

376
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,960
It's gonna be the framework for the rest of our talk.

377
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:21,720
He says, now that you know these things,

378
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:24,480
you will be blessed if you do them.

379
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:27,220
Knowing is this experiential understanding,

380
00:16:27,220 --> 00:16:28,560
this learning a lesson

381
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:30,440
from what Jesus has done before them.

382
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:32,640
We have to learn a lesson

383
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:34,200
about how much Jesus loves us,

384
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,760
about the service that he has done

385
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:37,180
in laying down his life for us

386
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,840
before we can ever go out

387
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:40,240
and serve others in the same way.

388
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:43,000
So he says, learn from me first this lesson

389
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,800
of what it means to serve in the kingdom.

390
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:48,240
Know these things deep inside your bones

391
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,660
and then once you understand this,

392
00:16:50,660 --> 00:16:53,400
do not serve before you understand

393
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,540
how much I have served you.

394
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:58,340
Come first to the table to see,

395
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:01,160
to experience and to know how much I love you

396
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:05,100
and then go out and do it for others also.

397
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,100
So first, let's look at this idea of knowing,

398
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,340
of learning, of teaching.

399
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:12,220
And teach is the word I have in my outline,

400
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:14,540
but it's probably not the best terminology here

401
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:16,540
because I think Jesus is performing

402
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,100
this act of sacrificial love

403
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:20,580
to help them understand both intellectually,

404
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:21,760
which is the idea of teach,

405
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:24,320
but also on an experiential level,

406
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,460
how much he loves them.

407
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:30,340
This is an object lesson of Christ's love for them

408
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:31,440
and for us.

409
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:34,420
It is intended to help us grasp at a guttural level

410
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:37,120
how high and how wide and how deep

411
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:39,760
is the love of Christ for us.

412
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:43,920
And if we truly learn this lesson,

413
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,840
we will serve others in the very same way

414
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:48,300
because our cup is full.

415
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:53,120
Genuine kingdom service comes out of the overflow

416
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,500
of the love that we have received from Jesus.

417
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:57,620
And he knows that as sinful, selfish,

418
00:17:57,620 --> 00:17:59,860
and broken people living in a broken world,

419
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:03,000
we are typically preoccupied with serving ourselves.

420
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,580
We are typically preoccupied with this scarcity mindset.

421
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:10,220
It's the fear that comes in in Genesis 3,

422
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,380
the sweat of the brow,

423
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,940
there isn't going to be enough for me and my people.

424
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:21,760
And Jesus knows that the tendency of the human heart

425
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:24,340
is to operate out of a scarcity mindset.

426
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,000
And I think the reason oftentimes

427
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,660
we either choose not to serve others sacrificially

428
00:18:30,660 --> 00:18:31,880
or choose to serve others

429
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,680
in order to get something out of it

430
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,860
is because we operate out of this scarcity mindset.

431
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:41,080
We're looking for love, we're longing for love.

432
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:42,600
And it's interesting to me,

433
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:47,560
if you interact with people

434
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:50,240
that are like emotionally unhealthy,

435
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,820
like outwardly doing things

436
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:54,380
where you can like Michael Scott, right?

437
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:57,760
He's like obvious to everyone around him

438
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,360
that he's doing this for the wrong reasons.

439
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,560
When you, typically my experience

440
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,220
is when I have interactions with people like that

441
00:19:04,220 --> 00:19:05,760
where you could just blatantly tell.

442
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,740
It's like, oh, you're doing this for you,

443
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:08,640
not for anybody else.

444
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:11,700
It's been my experience

445
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:14,280
that those people often were not loved well

446
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:18,160
as children or even currently,

447
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:20,440
that they're operating out of this scarcity mindset.

448
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:22,860
They want others to love them so bad

449
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:29,180
that they're acting in this unhealthy and bad way,

450
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:32,040
but deep down inside, they're crying for love.

451
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,240
And I think what Jesus is doing here

452
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,780
is he's teaching his disciples

453
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:38,380
that you are already far more loved

454
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,540
than you ever dare hope.

455
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:43,780
And if you can get this in your bones,

456
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:45,680
then you will be able to serve others

457
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,720
out of a, not a scarcity mindset,

458
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:50,360
but an abundance mindset

459
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:52,820
that you have more than enough love to give to others.

460
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:56,000
You have more than enough forgiveness to give to others.

461
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,360
You have more than enough grace to extend to others

462
00:19:58,360 --> 00:20:00,960
because grace has been extended to you

463
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:03,580
over and over and over again.

464
00:20:04,740 --> 00:20:09,040
We did this marriage content with Marissa a few years back

465
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:11,340
and I love the illustration they used.

466
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:12,640
I'll never forget about it.

467
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:16,020
They talked about how meeting each other's expectations

468
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:17,740
is really helpful for good communication.

469
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:21,160
And when unmet expectations haven't been communicated,

470
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,920
it's like you're stepping on your partner's air hose.

471
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,880
And so I don't know if you've ever been

472
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:28,980
in this type of interaction with a spouse before

473
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:32,260
or a partner where they're acting out

474
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:34,820
and you're like, whoa, like that's crazy.

475
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:36,540
But like they're acting out

476
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,000
because they're desperate for something

477
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,060
that you haven't given them.

478
00:20:39,060 --> 00:20:40,260
Maybe they haven't communicated it,

479
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:40,960
but it doesn't matter.

480
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:43,200
They need something from you and they don't have it.

481
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,460
And that thing that they don't have

482
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:45,680
feels like it's killing them.

483
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:48,400
And so when somebody steps on an air hose,

484
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:52,620
actions get pretty desperate, right?

485
00:20:52,620 --> 00:20:56,540
And I think oftentimes when we serve out of the wrong reason

486
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:57,960
or we don't serve at all,

487
00:20:57,960 --> 00:21:01,300
it's because we feel like we've gotta get ours for us.

488
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:03,180
And Jesus here in this example is saying,

489
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:05,140
you already have all that you need in me.

490
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:08,320
I have given you all that you need

491
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:12,200
to be full and to serve others.

492
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:19,760
We need to meditate on this reality,

493
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,960
actually learn this truth experientially

494
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:25,320
so that we have this abundant mindset

495
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:28,280
that we know we have more than enough to give to others.

496
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:30,840
I love how 1 John puts it, 1 John chapter four.

497
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:34,100
This is one of the disciples who was sitting at this table

498
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:37,400
who had learned this lesson experientially.

499
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:41,060
He said, this is how God showed us his love among us.

500
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:44,080
He sent his one and only son into the world

501
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:45,400
so that we might live through him.

502
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:47,880
This is love, not that we have loved God,

503
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:50,460
but that he has loved us and sent his son

504
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:52,500
as an atoning sacrifice for our sins.

505
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:56,600
We have to first and foremost realize

506
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:59,340
how much God has loved us in Jesus.

507
00:21:59,340 --> 00:22:02,700
I think John experientially learned this lesson

508
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,560
over the three years of Christ's ministry, yes,

509
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:07,180
but I think there's no more potent opportunity

510
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:09,500
for him to learn this lesson than in this upper room

511
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:11,840
when Jesus stood up to do the most audacious thing

512
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,200
that any rabbi would ever think to do.

513
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,940
John knew in his bones that Jesus loved him

514
00:22:17,940 --> 00:22:21,440
and because of that, he was willing to serve others.

515
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,880
Because he learned that lesson,

516
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:25,200
he was set up to serve others in the very same way.

517
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:28,180
And I would suggest to us this morning

518
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,220
that Jesus has invited us to serve others

519
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:32,300
in the same way that he has served us,

520
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,540
but before we can do that,

521
00:22:33,540 --> 00:22:37,240
we have to get this truth in our bones.

522
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,360
At an experiential level,

523
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:42,720
we have to learn the love of God for us

524
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:44,380
and it's so easy to forget.

525
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:46,500
I know this is like,

526
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:47,180
you guys are like,

527
00:22:47,180 --> 00:22:49,660
okay, you spent 20 minutes telling us Jesus loves us.

528
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:51,080
Can we move on to something else?

529
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:52,280
No, we can't.

530
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:55,500
We cannot move on past this

531
00:22:55,500 --> 00:22:56,960
until we get it in our bones

532
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:58,660
and we have an enemy that roars around

533
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:01,860
like a lion seeking to devour us and destroy us.

534
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:04,680
And I think the primary place that he attacks us

535
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,660
is this reality.

536
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:06,620
You are not love.

537
00:23:07,340 --> 00:23:08,660
You are not welcomed.

538
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:10,280
You have done too much.

539
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:11,640
You have walked away too far.

540
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,860
Do you know what you've done?

541
00:23:12,860 --> 00:23:14,000
Do you know where you've been?

542
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,400
Do you know who you are?

543
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:16,320
And Jesus says,

544
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,280
I stood up from the table

545
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:20,380
and I washed Judas' feet.

546
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:22,680
I love you.

547
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:30,840
No matter how much we've walked away,

548
00:23:30,840 --> 00:23:33,980
no matter how much we've abandoned Jesus,

549
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:36,920
he keeps extending his grace.

550
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:41,160
He wants us to know at an experiential level

551
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,300
how much he loves us

552
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:46,120
so that we can serve others out of an abundance mindset.

553
00:23:46,120 --> 00:23:47,860
So to get really practical here on this section,

554
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:50,380
a couple of things that I would encourage you

555
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:51,100
to think about doing.

556
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:52,340
The first is I would encourage you

557
00:23:52,340 --> 00:23:56,060
to think about reading John chapter 13 this week

558
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:58,720
a few times with an imaginative reading process,

559
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:00,140
kind of this Lectio Divina.

560
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:01,360
We've talked about it in the past,

561
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:04,260
but like do your best to just sit quietly

562
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:07,480
in a space where you have time and space

563
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:09,020
to just like be by yourself,

564
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,980
which I know for some of us who have toddlers

565
00:24:10,980 --> 00:24:12,080
is next to impossible,

566
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:13,440
but find a way.

567
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:19,320
And think about putting yourself in the room,

568
00:24:19,320 --> 00:24:22,540
sitting around the table,

569
00:24:22,540 --> 00:24:26,380
and just read this passage.

570
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:30,920
Think about the reality of how much God truly loves you.

571
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:33,720
Read it again and again and again

572
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:36,440
until it gets deep into your soul,

573
00:24:36,440 --> 00:24:39,040
until it's not just words on a page,

574
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:42,360
but it is a reality that Jesus is doing this for you.

575
00:24:42,360 --> 00:24:44,900
Second thing I would encourage you to do

576
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:45,960
is consider showing up

577
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:47,400
to the threefold communion service.

578
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,460
I know for many of us,

579
00:24:49,460 --> 00:24:52,400
that's like uncomfortable and weird

580
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:54,300
and very not culturally relevant,

581
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:57,800
but I will tell you from firsthand experience,

582
00:24:57,800 --> 00:24:59,380
it's one of the most powerful ways

583
00:24:59,380 --> 00:25:02,180
to truly just like learn this lesson.

584
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:04,160
It's an embodied spiritual practice.

585
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:06,100
We are whole human beings,

586
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:08,780
and oftentimes we handle discipleship

587
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:09,520
just in our heads.

588
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:12,940
And like I think Corey said this last week,

589
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:15,600
it's one thing to wash somebody else's feet.

590
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:17,020
You wanna learn this lesson

591
00:25:17,020 --> 00:25:19,100
about how much Jesus loves you.

592
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:22,060
You let another sinner wash your feet

593
00:25:22,060 --> 00:25:26,800
and then heighten that feeling that you have

594
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,140
to the point of Jesus,

595
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:29,980
the God who made you,

596
00:25:29,980 --> 00:25:31,120
who put breath in your lungs

597
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:32,900
doing that very action to you.

598
00:25:33,780 --> 00:25:36,780
It will totally reframe how you think about this.

599
00:25:36,780 --> 00:25:38,520
So consider that.

600
00:25:38,520 --> 00:25:43,120
Kingdom service looks like

601
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:48,180
first knowing fully what Jesus has done for you

602
00:25:48,180 --> 00:25:50,740
and then blessed are you

603
00:25:50,740 --> 00:25:52,820
if you do these things,

604
00:25:52,820 --> 00:25:53,820
if you follow my example.

605
00:25:53,820 --> 00:25:55,960
The next two verses in that first John passage

606
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:57,400
pick up on this idea.

607
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,100
Dear friends,

608
00:25:58,260 --> 00:26:00,140
since God so loved us

609
00:26:00,140 --> 00:26:02,100
because the God of the universe

610
00:26:02,100 --> 00:26:03,540
stepped up from the table

611
00:26:03,540 --> 00:26:06,240
and walked to your dirty, stinky feet

612
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:08,280
and washed them with his bare hands

613
00:26:08,280 --> 00:26:09,860
and wiped them dry

614
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,240
with a garment around his waist,

615
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:14,460
since God has so loved you,

616
00:26:14,460 --> 00:26:18,080
we also ought to love one another.

617
00:26:18,080 --> 00:26:20,900
No one has ever seen God,

618
00:26:20,900 --> 00:26:22,180
but if we love one another,

619
00:26:22,180 --> 00:26:23,200
God lives in us

620
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:25,780
and his love is made complete in us.

621
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,500
I love how Esau Macaulay puts it.

622
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:28,760
He said that kingdom service

623
00:26:28,760 --> 00:26:31,360
is an enacted parable of the gospel.

624
00:26:31,360 --> 00:26:33,440
When we do this,

625
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:34,360
when we step up

626
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:36,340
and serve others in sacrificial ways,

627
00:26:36,340 --> 00:26:38,000
when we lay down our priorities

628
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:38,800
and our preferences

629
00:26:38,800 --> 00:26:39,880
and our comfort

630
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:41,200
and when we serve others,

631
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,000
it is a way

632
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:43,720
in which we demonstrate the gospel

633
00:26:43,720 --> 00:26:45,400
to others around us.

634
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:47,620
No one has ever seen God.

635
00:26:47,620 --> 00:26:49,680
How often do we have this conversation

636
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:50,140
with people

637
00:26:50,140 --> 00:26:51,660
